# Production-Ready WhatsApp & AI Coordinator Widget Integration

This plan details the implementation of a vertically stacked floating widget group in the bottom-right corner of public-facing pages, comprising:
1. **WhatsApp Floating Icon & Automaton**: A WhatsApp button redirecting to `https://wa.me/919673000450` along with a backend Webhook endpoint (`/api/whatsapp/webhook`) that handles Meta WhatsApp Cloud API verification and processes incoming user messages using Gemini API (with a dedicated database-managed prompt `WHATSAPP_SYSTEM_PROMPT`).
2. **AI Coordinator Audio Agent Widget**: A voice call button that displays a sleek, glassmorphic card (360px–400px wide) upon pop-up. It initiates `Contact_agent.py` via LiveKit (generating WebRTC room guest tokens via `/api/livekit/token`) with the receptionist display layout, mute, toggle chat, audio visualizer, and message history.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The WhatsApp Meta Webhook requires three new environment variables in the backend server's `.env`:
> - `WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN`: A custom string token you set in your Meta App Dashboard Webhook configuration to verify subscription.
> - `WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN`: The permanent Meta system user access token or page token authorized to send WhatsApp messages back.
> - `WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID`: The unique phone number ID generated by Meta for your Business number.
> We will add placeholder fallbacks to prevent runtime crashes, but these must be configured in production for real messages to deliver.

