### Backend Server Changes

#### [NEW] [livekit.ts](file:///d:/Product%20Development/NxtGen_Academy/server/src/routes/livekit.ts)
Implement a public router for LiveKit token generation:
- Route: `GET /api/livekit/token?room=nxtgen-contact-room`
- Generates a signed guest WebRTC join token using `livekit-server-sdk` and credentials from environment variables (`LIVEKIT_API_KEY`, `LIVEKIT_API_SECRET`, `LIVEKIT_URL`), with a random candidate identity (`guest-...`).

#### [NEW] [whatsapp.ts](file:///d:/Product%20Development/NxtGen_Academy/server/src/routes/whatsapp.ts)
Implement the Meta WhatsApp Cloud API webhook router:
- Route: `GET /api/whatsapp/webhook`
  - Validates Meta's webhook subscription using `hub.mode`, `hub.verify_token`, and `hub.challenge` comparing against `WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN`.
- Route: `POST /api/whatsapp/webhook`
  - Parses incoming WhatsApp text messages from Meta payload.
  - Queries Gemini (using `gemini-1.5-flash`) grounded in `WHATSAPP_SYSTEM_PROMPT` retrieved from `SiteConfig` (with a short-text conversational fallback).
  - Posts the generated AI response back to the user via Meta Cloud API using `WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN` and `WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID`.

#### [MODIFY] [index.ts](file:///d:/Product%20Development/NxtGen_Academy/server/src/routes/index.ts)
Register `/api/livekit` and `/api/whatsapp` routers:
- Connect the new `livekitRouter` at `router.use('/livekit', livekitRouter)`.
- Connect the new `whatsappRouter` at `router.use('/whatsapp', whatsappRouter)`.

#### [MODIFY] [admin.ts](file:///d:/Product%20Development/NxtGen_Academy/server/src/routes/admin.ts)
- Update `GET /api/admin/about-us` to retrieve and include `WHATSAPP_SYSTEM_PROMPT` (with a high-quality short text fallback prompt).
- Update `POST /api/admin/about-us` to allow saving of `WHATSAPP_SYSTEM_PROMPT`.

